#: ../../build123d/docs/topology_selection.rst:3
msgid "Topology Selection and Exploration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build123d/docs/topology_selection.rst:5
msgid ":ref:`topology` is the structure of build123d geometric features, and traversing the topology of a part is often required to specify objects for an operation or to locate a CAD feature. In a GUI you would click on a feature; in code you describe it. That description has three parts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build123d/docs/topology_selection.rst:10
msgid "a :ref:`selector <selectors>` names the *kind* of feature - vertices, edges, wires, faces or solids - and returns them all in a |ShapeList|;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build123d/docs/topology_selection.rst:12
msgid ":ref:`operators <operators>` sort, group and filter that list, or slice it like any Python list, until what remains is the feature you meant;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build123d/docs/topology_selection.rst:14
msgid ":ref:`criteria <criteria>` are what the operators sort, group and filter *by*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../build123d/docs/topology_selection.rst:16
msgid "Criteria come in three kinds, and keeping them apart makes selectors easier to write:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build123d/docs/topology_selection.rst:18
msgid "**What a feature is.** Its own geometry: the type of curve or surface, its length, area, radius or volume, which way it points, where it lies. These are properties of the feature alone and can be measured with nothing else in hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../build123d/docs/topology_selection.rst:21
msgid "**How a feature sits in its shape.** Whether an edge is a convex or concave corner of the solid, which faces are its neighbours, which face a vertex was picked off. These are relations, not properties: the same straight edge is convex on a box and concave at the inner corner of an L, and nothing about the edge itself says which."
msgstr ""

#: ../../build123d/docs/topology_selection.rst:25
msgid "**When a feature came to be.** Whether the last operation created it, brought it in, or only rebuilt it. This is the feature's history, and it is what makes \"fillet the edges I just made\" possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../build123d/docs/topology_selection.rst:33
msgid "Selectors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build123d/docs/topology_selection.rst:35
msgid "Selectors extract all of a feature type from the referenced object, or the subset the last operation is responsible for. They are available on every ``Shape`` and on every builder, and return a |ShapeList|, a subclass of ``list`` that the :ref:`operators` refine."
msgstr ""

